            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Khao Sok National Park - bungalows on a misty morning</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Khao Sok National Park, Thailand
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          If you're planning a visit to Khao Sok National Park, welcome. Whether you're just beginning your research or counting down the days until you arrive, we hope this page helps you make the most of your visit.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Few places in Thailand capture the imagination quite like Khao Sok National Park. Ancient rainforest, towering limestone cliffs and remarkable wildlife combine to create one of the country's most extraordinary natural landscapes. It's a place to slow down, explore and reconnect with nature. Every trail, viewpoint and journey has a story waiting to be discovered.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          This page answers many of the questions we're asked by visitors every week. Along the way you'll find practical advice, local knowledge and a few of the small observations we've gathered from years of helping guests discover this remarkable place that we're fortunate enough to call home.
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Planning Your Visit</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Jump straight to the section you're looking for, or simply read on.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <a class="fusion-one-page-text-link guide-link" href="#where">&#x1f9ed; <strong>Where Is Everything?</strong></a><br /> Understand the layout of Khao Sok National Park and where the main attractions are located.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <a class="fusion-one-page-text-link guide-link" href="#natpark">&#x1f33f; <strong>What Makes Khao Sok National Park Unique?</strong></a><br /> Discover why this ancient rainforest is unlike anywhere else in Thailand.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <a class="fusion-one-page-text-link guide-link" href="#wildlife">&#x1f99c; <strong>Wildlife of Khao Sok National Park</strong></a><br /> Explore the remarkable animals and plants that thrive in this ancient rainforest.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <a class="fusion-one-page-text-link guide-link" href="#lake">&#x1f6a4; <strong>Exploring Cheow Lan Lake</strong></a><br /> Discover the history, scenery and unforgettable experiences of Cheow Lan Lake.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <a class="fusion-one-page-text-link guide-link" href="#besttime">&#x1f326;&#xfe0f; <strong>When Is the Best Time to Visit?</strong></a><br /> Learn how the changing seasons shape the Khao Sok experience.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <a class="fusion-one-page-text-link guide-link" href="#info">&#x2753; <strong>Practical Visitor Information</strong></a><br /> Quick answers to the questions visitors ask most before arriving in Khao Sok.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <a class="fusion-one-page-text-link guide-link" href="#history">&#x1f4d6; <strong>The History of Khao Sok National Park</strong></a><br /> Follow the remarkable story of how nature, people and conservation shaped the National Park.
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Where Is Everything?</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          One of the questions we're asked most often is surprisingly simple:
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <strong>"Where exactly is everything?"</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          It's a fair question. Khao Sok National Park is experienced through several distinct areas rather than a single entrance or visitor centre. The National Park Headquarters, Khao Sok Village, the Sok River, Cheow Lan Lake and Rajjaprabha Dam all play an important role in a visit to the park, but they are not all in the same place.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The map below shows how these key locations relate to one another, helping you understand the layout of Khao Sok National Park before you begin exploring.
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Understanding Khao Sok National Park</span>
        </h2>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Understanding-KS-Nat-Park-Map-NO-TITLE-2-scaled.jpg"
            alt="Map showing how far Khao Sok village is from Rajjaprabha Dam, the gateway to Cheow Lan lake"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Map showing how far Khao Sok village is from Rajjaprabha Dam, the gateway to Cheow Lan lake</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Understanding-KS-Nat-Park-Map-Mobile-34-v2.jpg"
            alt="Map showing how far Khao Sok village is from Rajjaprabha Dam, the gateway to Cheow Lan lake - mobile version"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Map showing how far Khao Sok village is from Rajjaprabha Dam, the gateway to Cheow Lan lake - mobile version</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <em>Khao Sok National Park is explored through two main gateways. Khao Sok Village is home to the National Park Headquarters and most accommodation, while Rajjaprabha Dam is the departure point for Cheow Lan Lake, floating bungalows and lake tours. The map also highlights one of the biggest surprises for first-time visitors: the Sok River lies outside the National Park boundary, even though many of Khao Sok's most popular river activities take place there.</em>
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Khao Sok at a Glance</span>
        </h2>
        <div class="my-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/70 shadow-md">
          <table width="100%"><colgroup><col /><col /></colgroup><thead style="background-color: #577810;"><tr><th align="left">Staying in Khao Sok Village<button class="swipe-arrow" type="button" aria-label="Show the next table column">➜</button></th><th align="left">Visiting Cheow Lan Lake</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left">Main gateway to the National Park</td><td align="left">Main gateway to the lake</td></tr><tr><td align="left">National Park Headquarters</td><td align="left">Rajjaprabha Dam Boat Pier</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Hotels, resorts & guesthouses</td><td align="left">Floating bungalow stays</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Restaurants, cafés, shops & pharmacy</td><td align="left">No towns or visitor facilities</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Hiking, river adventures & local experiences</td><td align="left">Boat tours, caves & wildlife safaris</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Canoeing, bamboo rafting & tubing</td><td align="left">Longtail boats & kayaking</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Village atmosphere</td><td align="left">Remote wilderness</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Ideal base for exploring Khao Sok</td><td align="left">Iconic day & overnight experience</td></tr></tbody></table>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Did you know?</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Many first-time visitors assume that Khao Sok Village sits beside Cheow Lan Lake. In fact, the two are around 64 km apart, connected by Route 401 through the southern edge of the National Park.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Most visitors stay in Khao Sok Village and travel to the lake for the day or as part of an overnight tour, making it easy to experience both sides of the National Park during the same visit.
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>What Makes Khao Sok National Park Unique?</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Khao Sok National Park is one of Thailand's most remarkable natural landscapes. Towering limestone mountains rise above ancient evergreen rainforest, while hidden caves and waterfalls reveal a landscape shaped over millions of years. The creation of Cheow Lan Lake in the 1980s added another distinctive feature, transforming part of the park into a maze of limestone islands and sheltered bays.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The rainforest is just as extraordinary. Scientists believe parts of Khao Sok are among the oldest continuously evolving evergreen rainforests on Earth.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Combined with a warm tropical climate and abundant rainfall, these forests support an exceptional variety of plants and wildlife. Tiny orchids grow alongside giant Rafflesia flowers, while hornbills, gibbons, elephants and the elusive clouded leopard all call this remarkable rainforest home.
        </p>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/new-khao-sok-national-park-13.jpg"
            alt="Misty view across the park"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Misty view across the park</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Although Khao Sok National Park covers 739 square kilometres, the rainforest extends far beyond its official boundaries. Together with neighbouring protected areas, including Khlong Phanom National Park, it forms one of Thailand's largest remaining protected rainforest landscapes.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          For wildlife and plants, there are no signposts or park boundaries. The rainforest continues long after the National Park boundary ends.
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Did you know?</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Parts of Khao Sok's evergreen rainforest are believed to be older than the Amazon. Having survived major climatic changes over millions of years, it is considered one of the oldest continuously evolving rainforests on Earth.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Now that you know how Khao Sok National Park is laid out and what makes it so special, let's take a closer look at the rainforest and the remarkable wildlife that calls it home.
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Wildlife of Khao Sok National Park</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          One of the greatest attractions of Khao Sok National Park is its extraordinary wildlife. Although sightings are never guaranteed, every visit offers the opportunity to experience one of Thailand's richest rainforest ecosystems.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The rainforest is home to an incredible variety of mammals, birds, reptiles, insects and plants. Visitors may be lucky enough to spot hornbills gliding between the limestone cliffs, hear white-handed gibbons calling through the forest canopy at dawn, or catch a glimpse of dusky langurs, macaques or colourful butterflies along a jungle trail.
        </p>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/hornbill.jpg"
            alt="Hornbill"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Hornbill</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Larger animals such as Asian elephants, tapirs and the elusive clouded leopard also inhabit the forest, although they are rarely seen. Their presence is a reminder that Khao Sok remains a genuinely wild landscape where nature still follows its own rhythms.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Wildlife is not confined to the National Park's hiking trails. The Sok River, Cheow Lan Lake and the forests surrounding Khao Sok Village all provide excellent opportunities to observe birds, reptiles and other rainforest species. Sometimes the most memorable encounters happen when you're simply sitting quietly and taking in your surroundings.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <a href="/khao-sok-jungle-thailand-rainforest/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Explore our Khao Sok Wildlife Guide <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Local Knowledge</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Guests often ask us what wildlife they are most likely to see. The honest answer is that every day is different. Some visitors are treated to hornbills flying overhead before breakfast, while others remember the haunting calls of gibbons echoing through the forest long after they have returned home. In Khao Sok, patience is often rewarded.
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Did you know?</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Rafflesia, the world's largest flower, grows naturally in Khao Sok National Park. It can reach almost one metre in diameter, blooms for only a few days and produces a distinctive scent that attracts insects for pollination.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          To learn more about the remarkable animals and plants that live here, explore our Khao Sok Wildlife Guide, where you'll find detailed information about mammals, birds, reptiles, insects and rainforest plants, along with the best places and activities for spotting them.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <a href="/khao-sok-jungle-thailand-rainforest/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Explore our Khao Sok Wildlife Guide <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Exploring Cheow Lan Lake</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Cheow Lan Lake lies at the heart of Khao Sok National Park. Towering limestone mountains and ancient rainforest surround its calm emerald waters. Longtail boats weave through narrow channels and hidden bays, revealing one of Thailand's most remarkable landscapes.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Although it looks completely natural today, Cheow Lan Lake is a man-made reservoir. It was created after the construction of Rajjaprabha Dam in the early 1980s. Flooding the Pasaeng River valley transformed the landscape into the maze of limestone islands visitors see today.
        </p>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Longtail-Banner-1500-1000.jpg"
            alt="Explore the beauty of Khao Sok"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Explore the beauty of Khao Sok</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The lake changed far more than the scenery. Before the reservoir was filled, five villages stood in the Pasaeng River valley. Their residents were carefully relocated, while homes, farms, schools and temples disappeared beneath the rising water. Today, that hidden landscape forms one of the most fascinating chapters in the history of Khao Sok National Park.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          One of the best ways to experience the lake is by staying in a floating bungalow. They are the only accommodation within Khao Sok National Park. Once the day boats return to the dam, the lake becomes quieter. Wildlife is often more active, and dawn brings mist drifting between the towering limestone mountains.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Whether you visit for a day or stay overnight, Cheow Lan Lake offers unforgettable experiences. Cruise beneath towering limestone cliffs, hike through ancient rainforest, swim in warm emerald water and watch for wildlife along the shoreline. Many tours also include a visit to one of the lake's impressive caves.
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Cheow Lan Lake at a Glance</span>
