        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <a href="/thailand-rainy-season-is-it-a-good-time-to-visit-khao-sok/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Is the Rainy Season a Good Time to Visit Khao Sok? <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Practical Visitor Information</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          A little preparation goes a long way in Khao Sok National Park. Most visitors need nothing more than comfortable footwear, lightweight clothing and a sense of adventure. Here are some of the questions we're asked most often before guests arrive.
        </p>
        <div class="my-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/70 shadow-md">
          <table width="100%"><colgroup><col /><col /></colgroup><thead style="background-color: #577810;"><tr><th align="left">Question <button class="swipe-arrow" type="button" aria-label="Show the next table column">➜</button></th><th align="left">Answer</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left">Is it safe to swim in Cheow Lan Lake?</td><td align="left">Yes. Swimming is one of the highlights of visiting Cheow Lan Lake and most tours include time to enjoy the water. Always follow your guide's advice and swim only in designated areas.</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Can I stay inside Khao Sok National Park?</td><td align="left">Yes. The only accommodation inside the National Park is on the floating bungalows at Cheow Lan Lake. All hotels, resorts and guesthouses are located outside the park boundaries.</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Do I need a guide to visit Khao Sok National Park?</td><td align="left">Most rainforest hikes and lake activities are enjoyed with an experienced guide. Some shorter trails near the National Park Headquarters can be explored independently.</td></tr><tr><td align="left">How many days should I spend in Khao Sok?</td><td align="left">We usually recommend at least three days. This gives you enough time to experience both the rainforest around Khao Sok Village and Cheow Lan Lake without feeling rushed.</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Can I see elephants in Khao Sok National Park?</td><td align="left">Wild elephants live in the National Park but are rarely seen. Most visitors are more likely to encounter hornbills, gibbons, macaques and other rainforest wildlife.</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Is Khao Sok suitable for families?</td><td align="left">Yes. Many activities are suitable for children, although some hikes and cave tours are better suited to older children and active families.</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Are there crocodiles in Cheow Lan Lake?</td><td align="left">No. There are no crocodiles in Cheow Lan Lake.</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Is the rainy season a good time to visit?</td><td align="left">Absolutely. The rainforest is at its greenest, waterfalls are at their most spectacular and many visitors consider it one of the best times to experience Khao Sok.</td></tr></tbody></table>
        </div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>The History of Khao Sok National Park</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The history of Khao Sok National Park is a remarkable story of ancient geology, tropical rainforest, conservation and human resilience. Millions of years of natural change, together with more recent events, have shaped the extraordinary landscape visitors experience today.
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Nature Creates Khao Sok</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Millions of years ago, much of southern Thailand lay beneath a shallow tropical sea where thick layers of limestone slowly formed. As the land rose, rivers and tropical rainfall gradually carved towering cliffs, caves and hidden valleys into the landscape.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Over time, one of the world’s oldest evergreen rainforests developed across these limestone mountains. The combination of ancient geology, abundant rainfall and a warm tropical climate created the remarkable environment visitors enjoy today.
        </p>
